 {"id":"fabro-1d94","title":"Enforce one edit per file path per tool batch","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-02T19:59:23.761Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T13:23:36.731Z","description":"Add one line to .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/implementer.md: at most one edit per file path per tool batch; sequence dependent edits across batches. In run 01M0TXPX09279433MGWSWPVVP4 the worker log showed 3 concurrent-write-to-same-file-in-one-batch serializing warnings for main.go, README.md, and fib_test.go. Expected effect: eliminates the write-lock warnings and the silent-ordering hazard they signal, at zero cost.","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
 {"id":"fabro-e4fa","title":"Tighten planner sd call economy","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-02T19:59:23.883Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T13:23:36.854Z","description":"In .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/planner.md, make the rule conditional and checkable (sd list only if sd ready output is truncated or lacks needed blocker info) and add sd ready --format json to the command table. In run 01M0TXPX09279433MGWSWPVVP4 planner@1 ran sd ready then sd list with byte-identical ~3.3 KB payloads, and used a --format flag on ready not listed in the table. Expected effect: one fewer tracker call and ~10 s less deliberation per cycle while keeping the no-invented-flags rule credible.","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
 {"id":"fabro-e702","title":"Require timeout_ms on compile/test shells and ban placeholder appends in implementer prompt","status":"open","type":"task","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-02T20:15:59.086Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T13:23:36.979Z","description":"In .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/implementer.md ('Your job this pass') add two hard rules: (a) any shell call that compiles or tests MUST pass timeout_ms of at least 60000 — run 01M0WWKAQCWZC0Q0JK019H0ZC7's chained append+gofmt+vet+test died at the default 10s with zero output (seq 163-164, 10,345ms, is_error), forcing a blind re-run; (b) never append placeholder code to fix later — the implementer appended a mangled placeholder test via heredoc, then head -n -28 cut the wrong lines leaving a dangling comment, costing ~48s and ~6 wasted calls (a third of its 149.5s stage). Expected effect: implementer pass ~100s instead of ~150s and the silent-timeout failure class eliminated.","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
-{"id":"fabro-6a5a","title":"Fix PR postlude: disable auto-merge and stop the failing PR-body model call","status":"open","type":"task","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-02T20:15:59.090Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T13:23:37.087Z","description":"In the run-spec pull_request block (see .fabro/project.toml [run.pull_request]) set auto_merge=false — the auto-merge GraphQL call deterministically fails ('Auto merge is not allowed for this repository') despite auto_merge=true — and fix or disable the PR-body LLM call, which failed ('No object generated: Failed to parse response as JSON', worker log 16:44:33 in run 01M0WWKAQCWZC0Q0JK019H0ZC7) and fell back to a skeleton. The postlude burned ~53s after the exit node finished (16:43:46 to 16:44:39), 18% of the 293s wall, and emits two warn-level failures every run. Expected effect: run completes ~50s sooner with two fewer recurring warnings. Partial overlap with open fabro-9f97 (journal-only-diff case); this covers real-diff runs.","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
+{"id":"fabro-6a5a","title":"Fix PR postlude: disable auto-merge and stop the failing PR-body model call","status":"in_progress","type":"task","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-02T20:15:59.090Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-09T18:32:10.205Z","description":"In the run-spec pull_request block set auto_merge=false — the auto-merge GraphQL call deterministically fails ('Auto merge is not allowed for this repository') despite auto_merge=true — and fix or disable the PR-body LLM call, which failed ('No object generated: Failed to parse response as JSON', worker log 16:44:33 in run 01M0WWKAQCWZC0Q0JK019H0ZC7) and fell back to a skeleton. The postlude burned ~53s after the exit node finished (16:43:46 to 16:44:39), 18% of the 293s wall, and emits two warn-level failures every run. Expected effect: run completes ~50s sooner with two fewer recurring warnings. Partial overlap with open fabro-9f97 (journal-only-diff case); this covers real-diff runs. BASIS: run 01M0WWKAQCWZC0Q0JK019H0ZC7 review .fabro/reviews/develop/01M0WWKAQCWZC0Q0JK019H0ZC7.md. PATH CORRECTION (planner, 2026-09-09): the [run.pull_request] block does NOT live in .fabro/project.toml — it lives in .fabro/workflows/develop/workflow.toml (auto_merge = true at ~line 53, model = zai:glm-4.7 at ~line 58; note the run-spec default moved from project.toml into workflow.toml). The PR-body generation code is lib/components/fabro-workflow/src/pipeline/pull_request.rs (FALLBACK_BODY_NOTICE ~line 55, generation-failure fallback ~lines 488-512); the reviewer also noted the failure log named model=glm-5.3 while the spec configures zai:glm-4.7 — reconcile the model mismatch when fixing.","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
 {"id":"fabro-a23f","title":"Make implementer journal report errored or timed-out tool calls","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-02T20:16:05.689Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T13:23:37.192Z","description":"In .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/implementer.md (Journal section) add: a tool call that errored or timed out ALWAYS goes in observations, even when recovered — name the call, the timeout, and the workaround. Run 01M0WWKAQCWZC0Q0JK019H0ZC7's implementer journaled observations as none (seq 187) despite a 10.3s shell timeout, an is_error grep, and a signature change forcing edits at ~28 test call-sites; the signal reached the improve loop only via event-stream archaeology. Complements open fabro-b809 (mandatory painpoints array). Expected effect: friction self-reports on the run where it happens, so prompt fixes surface through the journal pipeline instead of manual analysis.","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
 {"id":"fabro-8d2c","title":"Raise preamble_budget_kb from 24 to 32 — evidence blob detour persists","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-02T20:16:05.701Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T13:23:37.295Z","description":"In .fabro/workflows/develop/workflow.fabro (graph attr, currently 24 after the 12-to-24 raise) set preamble_budget_kb=32. Run 01M0WWKAQCWZC0Q0JK019H0ZC7's 22.1KB evidence capture (seq 209) still rendered as a blob ref in the reviewer prompt (seq 218) because 22.9KB + tester section + context keys (~28KB aggregate) exceeds 24KB; the reviewer recovered via one 102ms read_file, but the same detour produced the false rejection in run 01M0SS23MJM8972CBJD0SP7T4Q. Expected effect: evidence arrives inline in the preamble, one fewer tool round-trip per review, preview-misread mode removed. SUPERSEDES the targets of open seeds fabro-83f9 and fabro-35ab (both still say raise from 12) — close or amend those to avoid triple filing.","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
 {"id":"fabro-f4cd","title":"Fast-path planner to sd show when the goal names a seed id","status":"closed","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-02T20:16:14.678Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-05T11:00:10.279Z","description":"In .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/planner.md step 1 add: if the goal names a seed id, run sd show <id> directly; run sd ready only when it doesn't, and never run sd list to re-confirm a count sd ready already printed. Run 01M0WWKAQCWZC0Q0JK019H0ZC7's goal named fabro-f74b; sd ready returned exactly that one seed (seq 39), yet the planner still ran sd list --format json purely to double-check the count (reasoning at seq 67), after sd show + sd update + two globs + a full 10.4KB read of main.go — 7 tool calls and 76.6s inference for a single-candidate claim. Expected effect: two fewer shell calls and one LLM turn on named-seed runs, the common case for this workflow's goals. Overlaps the tracker-empty case in open fabro-b382 and fabro-e4fa; this covers the named-seed case.","labels":["revision"],"closedAt":"2026-09-05T11:00:10.279Z","closeReason":"Superseded by fabro-7e88 (implemented in cycle 3, PR #25, e5f82da6c): same change — fast-path sd show when the goal names a seed id. Revisor journal of run 01M1RJVKW9 flagged the dangling duplicate; closed by the revisor-revisor pass (iterate skill, 2026-09-05)."}
